 "equipment_type": "Pressure-independent control valve with energy meter",
 "applies_to": "Belimo Energy Valve generation 3 (EV..R+(K)BAC, EV..R3+BAC, EV..F+(K)BAC), the installed base before Energy Valve V4.",
 "summary": "The Energy Valve V3 is a pressure-independent characterized control valve with a flow sensor and two temperature sensors, so it reports flow, delta T, power and heating/cooling energy. It talks BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP. AO 1 is a % setpoint read as position, flow or power depending on ControlMode (MV 100); the setpoint only follows the bus when SpSource (MV 122) is Bus.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Application 03.02-0000, firmware 12.25",
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "This is the older V3 object map; Energy Valve V4 uses a different, larger list.",
  "Flow, power and energy are each published in several units (l/min, m³/h, gpm, l/s, l/h; kW, kBTU/h, ton; kWh, MJ, kBTU, ton·h).",
  "AI 100 ErrorState bits: 0 sensor T1, 1 sensor T2, 2 flow sensor, 3 actuator cannot move, 4 flow with closed valve, 5 air bubbles, 6 flow not reached, 7 power not realized, 8 gear disengaged, 9 reverse flow, 10 MP communication faulty, 11 freeze warning.",
  "Value ranges may be limited further by the valve size (DN); see the product datasheet.",
  "Binary objects print state texts as 1/2 (No/Yes, OK/Not OK, None/Reset); kept as printed. BV 100 is printed with read access.",
  "Names printed with superscripts are written out here (AbsFlow_m3h for 'AbsFlow_m³h', V'max for V' with subscript max)."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet interface description, Energy Valve V3",
